From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: less fixed GPU memory on small GPUs

Invincible VS (PPSA30568) runs out of GPU memory on the PS4 Pro, which has
about 3 GB for the GPU in all. Two buffers KytyPS5 keeps for itself took
768 MB of that:

- The upload staging ring was 512 MB. With under 8 GB of device-local memory
  it is now 128 MB. Uploads that do not fit already take one-time buffers,
  and WriteDataBuffer already splits writes into ring-sized pieces.
- The tiler's two scratch buffers grew to the largest image ever converted
  and stayed (256 MB for a 16384x2048 array). They now stay only up to
  64 MB; a larger conversion gets a buffer freed once its submit completes.

diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
index 1e64234..e4ca0d8 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,20 @@ constexpr uint64_t GdsBufferSize = 64 * 1024;
 // GPU-modified ranges come as many small scattered islands, so a readback widens to a window.
 constexpr uint64_t DownloadWindowSize = 512 * 1024;
 
+// The staging ring is host memory the GPU reads. With under 8 GB of device-local memory (the
+// PS4's GPU has about 3 GB in all) 512 MB of it is too much; larger uploads take one-time
+// buffers and WriteDataBuffer splits writes into ring-sized pieces.
+uint64_t StagingSize(const GraphicContext& graphics) {
+	const auto& properties = graphics.physical_device_memory_properties;
+	uint64_t    local      = 0;
+	for (uint32_t heap = 0; heap < properties.memoryHeapCount; heap++) {
+		if (properties.memoryHeaps[heap].flags & vk::MemoryHeapFlagBits::eDeviceLocal) {
+			local += properties.memoryHeaps[heap].size;
+		}
+	}
+	return local < 8192 * MiB ? 128 * MiB : 512 * MiB;
+}
+
 std::pair<Buffer*, uint64_t> UploadMemory(GraphicContext& graphics, CommandScheduler& scheduler,
                                         StreamBuffer& staging, uint64_t size, uint64_t alignment,
                                         vk::BufferUsageFlags usage, const auto& write) {
@@ -243,7 +257,7 @@ BufferCache::BufferCache(GraphicContext& graphics, CommandScheduler& scheduler,
                                                             : MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal,
                              0, AllFlags, BDA_PAGETABLE_SIZE),
       m_memory_tracker(page_manager),
-      m_staging_buffer(graphics, scheduler, MemoryUsage::Upload, 512 * MiB),
+      m_staging_buffer(graphics, scheduler, MemoryUsage::Upload, StagingSize(graphics)),
       m_stream_buffer(graphics, scheduler, MemoryUsage::Stream, 64 * MiB),
       m_download_buffer(graphics, scheduler, MemoryUsage::Download, 64 * MiB),
       m_device_buffer(graphics, scheduler, MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal, 128 * MiB),
